<tr><td>International Existing Building Code (IEBC)</td><td>2021</td><td>How much upgrading a repair or alteration of an existing building triggers</td></tr>
<tr><td>International Energy Conservation Code (IECC)</td><td>2021</td><td>Insulation, windows, and air sealing when those components are replaced</td></tr>
<tr><td>International Property Maintenance Code (IPMC)</td><td>2021</td><td>Minimum condition standards for existing buildings</td></tr>
<tr><td>Mechanical, Plumbing, and Fuel Gas Codes (IMC, IPC, IFGC)</td><td>2021</td><td>HVAC, water, drain, and gas lines replaced after fire, freeze, or water losses</td></tr>
<tr><td>International Fire Code (IFC)</td><td>2021, as amended</td><td>Fire protection items, mostly on commercial and multifamily properties</td></tr>
<tr><td>International Swimming Pool and Spa Code (ISPSC)</td><td>2021</td><td>Pool and spa repairs, such as after a tree falls into a pool enclosure</td></tr>
<tr><td>National Electrical Code (NEC)</td><td>2020, as amended or as adopted by the State of Texas</td><td>Wiring replaced when walls are opened after fire or water damage</td></tr>
</tbody>
