<h2>Local amendments that affect insurance repairs</h2>
<p>Three of the city’s amendments come up regularly when a property is being repaired after a loss:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Reroofing.</strong> The city added the same exemption to both the IBC and the IRC: “Roof covering replacement permits are not required unless the weight of the replacement roof is heavier than the existing roof covering.”</li>
<li><strong>Foundations.</strong> All foundations must be designed by a licensed engineer, who submits a sealed letter of conformance. That can matter when a claim involves a foundation damaged by a fallen tree, a fire, or a covered plumbing leak.</li>
<li><strong>Extraterritorial jurisdiction (ETJ).</strong> A project in the city’s ETJ that receives City of San Marcos water, wastewater, or electric service must obtain a building permit, even though it is outside city limits.</li>
</ul>

